  "description": "DEBVOZ crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C182 H130 Ce6 Mn12 O69,10(C1 H3 N1 O2),8(C1 H2 Cl2). From the CIF bond table, Ce1 (Ce) has 9 O neighbors; Ce2 (Ce) has 9 O neighbors; Ce3 (Ce) has 9 O neighbors; Ce4 (Ce) has 9 O neighbors; Ce5 (Ce) has 9 O neighbors; Ce6 (Ce) has 9 O neighbors; Mn1 (Mn) has 6 O neighbors; Mn2 (Mn) has 6 O neighbors; Mn3 (Mn) has 5 O neighbors; Mn4 (Mn) has 6 O neighbors; Mn5 (Mn) has 6 O neighbors; Mn6 (Mn) has 5 O neighbors; Mn7 (Mn) has 6 O neighbors; Mn8 (Mn) has 6 O neighbors; Mn9 (Mn) has 5 O neighbors; Mn10 (Mn) has 6 O neighbors; Mn11 (Mn) has 6 O neighbors; Mn12 (Mn) has 5 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 51 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.019-5.266 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 88.94-179.52°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Ce6Mn12O17(O2CPh)26].",
